SCST_BIO AIX Device ODM Package - v2.0.0.0 RC1
=================================================

Purpose
-------
This is a vendor-style AIX/VIOS Device ODM package for SCST_BIO Fibre Channel
LUNs. Unlike the v1.x kit, it does NOT inject SCST_BIO into IBM's generic
disk/fcp/mpioosdisk model table.

It creates independent device identities:

  disk/fcp/scstmpio
  PCM/friend/scstmpio

The device still reuses IBM AIX native components:

  DvDr      = scsidisk
  Configure = /usr/lib/methods/cfgscsidisk
  PCM DvDr  = aixdiskpcmke
  PCM cfg   = aixdiskpcmrtl

Expected result
---------------
  # lsdev -Cc disk
  hdiskN Available ... SCST MPIO FC Disk

  # lsdev -l hdiskN -F 'name:uniquetype:description'
  hdiskN:disk/fcp/scstmpio:SCST MPIO FC Disk

  # lsmpio -l hdiskN
  ... multiple fscsi paths for the same hdisk ...

Recognition
-----------
Primary vendor-only model_map:
  0808SCST_BIO

Two exact fallback maps are also included for the currently observed Product IDs:
  0818SCST_BIOvios
  0818SCST_BIOaix72

Page 0x83 identity is used:
  unique_id values = 081083

Defaults
--------
Disk:
  queue_depth=32
  reserve_policy=no_reserve
  rw_timeout=30
  lun_reset_spt=yes

PCM:
  algorithm=shortest_queue
  hcheck_interval=60
  hcheck_cmd=test_unit_rdy
  hcheck_mode=nonactive
  timeout_policy=fail_path

No cfgmgr Config_Rules tuning hook is used. Defaults live directly in PdAt.

Build
-----
Run on AIX or VIOS in oem_setup_env:

  ./build.sh

Requires mkinstallp (bos.adt.insttools) and gencat.

Important test procedure
------------------------
1. Back up ODM and ensure the test hdisk is not in use.
2. Build and preview the image:
     cd payload/tmp
     inutoc .
     installp -L -d .
     installp -apd . devices.fcp.disk.SCST.mpio.rte
3. Install:
     installp -aXgd . devices.fcp.disk.SCST.mpio.rte
4. Verify predefined ODM:
     /usr/lpp/scst_mpio/bin/scst_mpio_check
5. Existing SCST hdisks keep their current PdDvLn. To test the new type, safely
   undefine the old test hdisk(s) and rediscover with cfgmgr/cfgdev.
6. Verify:
     lsdev -Cc disk
     lsdev -l hdiskN -F 'name:uniquetype:description'
     lsattr -El hdiskN
     lsmpio -l hdiskN

Safety
------
- The installer never removes configured hdisks.
- Deinstall refuses to remove ODM support while disk/fcp/scstmpio CuDv objects
  still exist.
- The v1 generic SCST_BIO mpio_model_map and its Config_Rules tuning hook are
  removed during v2 installation to prevent generic mpioosdisk from winning
  device selection.
- This is custom lab/vendor integration and is not IBM-certified storage support.

RC1 validation focus
--------------------
The key item to prove on the VIOS test system is that cfgscsidisk selects
disk/fcp/scstmpio from the vendor-only model_map (0808SCST_BIO). If it does not,
the exact 0818 Vendor+Product fallback entries should be tested next.
